growth-without-threshold+merge-losing-identity+split-creating-overlap+retire-with-live-consumer+pending-as-active+domain-self-registration+permission-sovereign-changing-domain-content+signature-self-assertion+plaintext-Chinese-mirror+verified-release-with-open-gate\nNo emergency administrator debug development performance or convenience condition may bypass an activation external-signature or Chinese-confidentiality gate', E'b3a304af81496aca27b8119808896dc672baaadfd63a446767f1be82d3bcba35', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D47', E'CODEX_MODULE_TEST', E'CODEX_TEST_VALIDATION_EVALUATION_SPECIAL_LAW', E'coverage-test-and-special-law-conflict-closure', E'coverage-test-and-special-law-conflict-closure\nSCOPE:all permission-sovereign directories+new fault/manual contracts+all special-law overlaps; DIRECTORY-COVERAGE:each master catalog entry has explicit required scope+exact completion rule+machine-readable zero-gap evidence+release gate regardless active or pending state; TEST-COVERAGE:every newly registered fault and maintenance manual maps to at least one test flow with fixtures expected results evidence cleanup isolation and timeout; SPECIAL-LAW-CONFLICT:every special law declares precedence against each materially overlapping law and denial preservation identity permission and evidence requirements may only become stricter; ACTIVATION:pending directories remain nonphysical until acceptance evidence exists; TRACE:provision>fault>manual>test>evidence and provision>special-law>conflict-rule shall be resolvable without free-text inference; REVIEW:on every directory law fault manual test or scope change recompute coverage and overlap matrices\nFORBID:directory-without-coverage-contract+fault-or-manual-without-test-flow+special-law-material-overlap-without-precedence+test-without-cleanup/isolation/timeout+coverage-by-sample-only+average-only-performance-acceptance+pending-as-active+conflict-resolved-by-owner-rank-outside-codex+free-text-only-traceability\nExternal signature and 星澄 confidential-storage gates retain their separate external evidence requirements and are not completed by coverage tests alone.', E'fe92d1e03d4274d23fa7f4a24b64863f639aefad9e77b999be927c1b9c58df74', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D48', E'CODEX_MODULE_TEST', E'CODEX_TEST_VALIDATION_EVALUATION_SPECIAL_LAW', E'activation-evidence-deadline-reference', E'activation-evidence-deadline-reference\nACTIVATION-EVIDENCE:startup completion is evaluated against PARAM[STARTUP_COMPLETE_DEADLINE_MS] and current runtime profile;VERSION:current Codex binding required\nFORBID:stale-deadline-literal+activation-without-current-evidence\nNormative cryptographic constants, identity formats and closed status enums remain explicit when variability would weaken interoperability or safety.', E'5371cf93cbbaceb050917a0448b3e21532771880d33c1121b0eac665d00a2237', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D49', E'CODEX_MODULE_TEST', E'CODEX_TEST_VALIDATION_EVALUATION_SPECIAL_LAW', E'complete-global-registry-traceability-and-routing', E'complete-global-registry-traceability-and-routing\nEvery active fault code command code and maintenance manual code shall appear verbatim in governed test evidence and resolve through immutable directory relationships. Every fault has an owner and specific manual or a global containment-routing manual with no generic mutation power. Every command has canonical identity owner schemas permission idempotency timeout route and typed result. Every manual has faults preconditions steps verification rollback stop conditions risk permission and tests. Independent discovery scans every producer consumer store log UI environment script and contract; any change invalidates evidence until the complete zero-gap graph reruns.\nFORBID:partial-inventory+sample-only-coverage+fault-without-routing+command-without-test+manual-without-test+global-manual-as-blanket-mutation-authority+free-text-identity+layer-alias+unknown-pass-through+registry-only-self-attestation+stale-coverage\nGlobal containment may route and isolate but cannot authorize source data permission release or lifecycle mutation without its specific sovereign chain.', E'08ebd25cab6083e63479db74616cb2d18d0c7ae1c2fcb8c5b1ea3dd0c99312eb', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D5', E'CODEX_MODULE_FOUNDATION', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'amendment-execution', E'amendment-execution\nAMENDMENT-EXEC:full-file-replacement; VERSION:system-auto-increment-decimal-5-fractional-digits; SIGN:deliberate-governor-act; RE-SEAL:immediate-after-replacement; READONLY:restore-before-any-load\nFORBID:partial-patch/version-skip/unsealed-load\n', E'78bfa0972591af720022b33b87e9ff2d8c1347de630e0cbeb4bd2c6f32dd42c1', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D50', E'CODEX_MODULE_DIRECTORY', E'CODEX_DIRECTORY_SPECIAL_LAW', E'complete-command-contract-and-sovereign-effectivity-closure', E'complete-command-contract-and-sovereign-effectivity-closure\nSCOPE:every command-code-directory entry and every active sovereign provision; COMMAND-COMPLETE:immutable command code+canonical command id/name+owner+domain+action+target+versioned input contract+versioned output contract+permission action+idempotency policy+timeout policy+introduced/retired version are all nonempty and exact; CONTRACT-NAMING:canonical-name-request-vN and canonical-name-result-vN unless a stricter registered schema identity exists; PERMISSION-ACTION:explicit action:target identity and never blank or inferred from display name; VALIDATION:registration+build+startup+dispatch+test+release reject any blank ambiguous duplicate incompatible or unversioned field; CHANGE:contract semantic change creates successor version and compatibility window; EFFECTIVITY:every active principle article edict and sovereign identity has one effective-provisions record while superseded provisions have none; ROOT-ARCHITECTURE:project root parent is explicitly null and is not missing data; EVIDENCE:complete directory scan+schema resolution+permission resolution+idempotency/timeout tests+effective/lineage parity\nFORBID:blank-input/output/permission+implicit-schema+display-name-permission+unversioned-contract+same-contract-id-different-semantics+dispatch-before-validation+active-sovereign-without-effective-record+superseded-provision-still-effective+root-null-parent-treated-as-error\nA truly payload-free command still uses a versioned empty-object request contract and typed result contract; blank strings are never valid.', E'223ddd57984cfe570276b44bf0dafdda20329230aa7892a31c9cca3c915b8bfd', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D51', E'CODEX_MODULE_TEST', E'CODEX_TEST_VALIDATION_EVALUATION_SPECIAL_LAW', E'complete-seal-timestamp-trust-and-component-evidence', E'complete-seal-timestamp-trust-and-component-evidence\nSCOPE:every sealed Codex successor version. EACH-VERSION:seal manifest+revision history head+certification evidence+registered trust anchor+timestamp record+sealed component manifest share the exact version identity. CERTIFICATION:the current governed authorization model uses deterministic integrity seal,lineage closure,registered authorization and atomic publication; current status is sealed-governed-authorization. COMPONENTS:policy,history,identities,lineage,metadata,provisions,schema,ownership,supersession and version rules bind the full root. FAILURE:missing,mismatched,blank or fabricated evidence remains fail-closed and cannot be marked sealed.\nFORBID:fabricated-certification+self-issued-unregistered-authorization+status-diverging-from-current-seal+seal-with-missing-component+retrospective-falsification\nRetrospective records may close structural evidence presence only; they do not establish original event time or satisfy the external human signature threshold.', E'b15e58f895dd834d976b9b7436caece5fae33794ed4fc251bc461592288cf6ef', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D52', E'CODEX_MODULE_RELEASE', E'CODEX_RELEASE_VERSION_SPECIAL_LAW', E'human-governor-manual-version-baseline-reset', E'human-governor-manual-version-baseline-reset\nAUTHORITY:explicit human-governor amendment; ACTION:set current codex version manually to 1.00000 as a new natural-evolution baseline; PRESERVATION:record previous version+history head+content root+identity root+full root before reset and retain all revision history+provision identities+lineage+supersession evidence; CURRENT-SEAL:1.00000 seal is regenerated for the complete integrated current codex and supersedes the former baseline seal without deleting its recorded predecessor roots; FUTURE:every successor after this reset derives naturally from 1.00000 under the highest applicable change degree and cannot be manually changed again without another explicit human-governor amendment; CERTIFICATION:external offline signatures remain required; COMMAND:explicit user command is lawful one-time authority for this E2 baseline reset; CONSUMPTION:command was consumed by H045 and cannot be replayed duplicated or converted into standing reset permission; COMPLIANCE:an explicit authenticated user one-time command is compliant when scope+single-use nonce+consumption record+authority+evidence are valid; the H045 reset command satisfies these conditions and is fully consumed; COMPLIANCE-VERDICT:H045 user one-time reset command is compliant+lawful+fully consumed and cannot be replayed\nFORBID:automatic-version-reset+silent-reset+history/identity/lineage-deletion+unrecorded-predecessor-root+version-change-by-runtime/repair/update/tool+verified-status-without-external-signatures+replay-consumed-user-reset-command+rejecting-valid-consumed-one-time-user-command-as-noncompliant\nThis one reset is authorized only by the explicit human-governor instruction recorded in H045; it creates no standing automatic reset power.', E'a7631f7777f80ac76c2dc9dc9becbd23d9a0ee67c0483f46ea5f76884ec461e9', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D53', E'CODEX_MODULE_RELEASE', E'CODEX_RELEASE_VERSION_SPECIAL_LAW', E'version-epoch-identity-and-natural-evolution', E'version-epoch-identity-and-natural-evolution\nVERSION-IDENTITY:{epoch,display-version}; CURRENT:E2:1.00000; UNIQUENESS:display version may repeat only across different immutable epochs and every history+seal+revision+signature reference resolves the epoch-qualified identity; RESET:explicit human-governor creates a new epoch after recording predecessor version+history head+all roots; FUTURE:within E2 successors naturally apply highest change degree once and no automatic reset exists; RESET-COMMAND:the explicit user command consumed by H045 lawfully created E2 and has no remaining execution authority\nFORBID:unqualified-version-identity+two-current-epochs+overwrite-predecessor-evidence+automatic/silent-reset+history-deletion\nLegacy tables may retain display-version fields only when current_version_identity supplies the mandatory epoch qualifier.', E'46ae55905e5ff890d5225fa2fc7f3053ab38fbd251ccfc4a056bb85b63690191', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D54', E'CODEX_MODULE_FOUNDATION', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'mandatory-declaration-and-implementation-force', E'mandatory-declaration-and-implementation-force\nFORCE:every enacted codex declaration creates a mandatory implementation obligation unless explicitly declared non-operational; DEFAULT:no declaration is advisory; SEPARATION:declaration may precede implementation but implementation remains compulsory; ACTIVATION:verified completion and affected release remain blocked until evidence satisfies the obligation; DELEGATION:detailed fields+lifecycle+deadlines+verification+waiver are governed by D55\nFORBID:advisory-by-default+declaration-without-enforceable-obligation+silent-waiver+completion-without-evidence+release-with-open-blocking-obligation\nOnly an explicit human-governor successor law may cancel or replace an obligation while preserving lineage.', E'1a1770dd9e702ae93e1f110d2004fc3e79e56ea66cdc34e4246612fc2855b700', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D55', E'CODEX_MODULE_DIRECTORY', E'CODEX_IMPLEMENTATION_OBLIGATION_SPECIAL_LAW', E'mandatory-implementation-obligation-special-law', E'mandatory-implementation-obligation-special-law\nDIRECTORY:implementation-obligation registry owned by permission-sovereign; ENTRY:obligation-code+source-provision+implementation-owner+target-state+current-state+created-at+due-at+previous-state+verification-owner+acceptance-evidence+noncompliance-effect+escalation+waiver-rule; LIFECYCLE:mandated>planned>in-progress>evidence-submitted>verified>complete or failed/escalated/superseded; DEADLINE:every open obligation has exact UTC due-at and next escalation; MANAGEMENT:domain owner implements+health-maintenance-test-sub-sovereign verifies+permission-sovereign registers; FORCE:overdue or failed obligation remains visible and blocks affected activation+verified release; WAIVER:human-governor successor law only\nFORBID:ownerless-or-deadline-free-obligation+permanent-pending+state-skip+same-actor-implement-and-final-verify+evidence-free-complete+automatic-waiver+deletion+unrelated-test-as-proof\nA deadline may be extended only once by explicit recorded human-governor decision before expiry, with reason and successor due-at.', E'93352774f4bf07ae7587d90ed7d860d4ca429e6dbf35bfeb56b8df5a36de7ddb', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D56', E'CODEX_MODULE_XINGCHENG', E'CODEX_STAR_PRIVILEGED_INSTITUTION_SPECIAL_LAW', E'星澄-audit-inspection-capability-strengthening', E'星澄-audit-inspection-capability-strengthening\nROLE:星澄 is an independent read-only global audit inspector and never a governance+permission+system+maintenance decision sovereign; SCOPE:official codex+permission-sovereign managed directories+architecture+identity+commands+faults+manuals+tests+implementation obligations+release+runtime health+channels+events+state+PostgreSQL/Rust-Vector-Engine evidence views through information-layer; ACCESS:permission-review-exempt for registered 星澄 identity but still requires official-entry authentication+purpose binding+read-only single-use session+scope+nonce+expiry+audit; POWERS:cross-directory consistency inspection+gap/conflict/drift detection+seal/version/lineage verification+fault pattern correlation+stability/performance/isolation/jailbreak evidence review+independent acceptance challenge+typed noncompliance finding; OUTPUT:finding-code+scope+evidence references+severity+affected authority+required response+deadline recommendation without secret payload; REMEDIATION:none direct and finding routes to responsible sovereign through information-layer; CONFIDENTIALITY:星澄 identity+exclusive directory+Chinese codex+private findings never disclosed exported mirrored or delegated; INDEPENDENCE:no inspected owner may alter suppress or self-close 星澄 finding\nFORBID:星澄-direct-write+code/data/directory/permission mutation+execution/delegation+final policy decision+private database/socket/tool access+finding-without-evidence+secret-in-finding+identity/directory/Chinese-codex disclosure+finding suppression+inspected-owner-self-close+audit-session replay\n星澄 may request a new scoped evidence view or challenge an acceptance verdict; the responsible sovereign retains decision authority and health-maintenance-test-sub-sovereign retains verification management.', E'96fc602aba60f68c05f7090f286b7e4a1f83f0fdccb56814623591c93a0baa3f', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D57', E'CODEX_MODULE_TEST', E'CODEX_TEST_VALIDATION_EVALUATION_SPECIAL_LAW', E'whole-codex-integrity-and-gap-closure-special-law', E'whole-codex-integrity-and-gap-closure-special-law\nSCOPE:the complete Codex database, confidential Chinese mirror, identities, lineage, revisions, lifecycle, classifications, directories, references, sovereign topology, duty limits, version epoch, history chain and seals; REQUIRED-CHECKS:schema+primary identity uniqueness+position uniqueness where ordered+exact registry mirror parity+semantic provision mirror equivalence+all active provision registry closure+superseded provision exclusion from effective set+reference resolution+acyclic parent and supersession graphs+single canonical authority/name+ASCII machine alias resolution+single-parent sub-sovereigns+maximum three duties per sub-sovereign with single-duty preference+decision/delegation/execution separation+privileged institution boundary+special-law conflict closure+version and seal reproducibility+confidentiality and anti-jailbreak controls; CONTRADICTION:compare permissions, prohibitions, exceptions, precedence, ownership and execution powers across every applicable law; RESULT:each check emits pass/fail/not-applicable with exact identity and evidence hash; FAILURE:any unresolved mismatch, orphan, stale mirror, ambiguous precedence, broken seal, unauthorized legacy identity or contradictory active rule blocks certification and publication; REPAIR:only the exact defective record may be amended under authorization, preserving history and unrelated work; COMPLETION:zero unresolved defects and independently reproducible roots\nFORBID:sample-only audit+identity-only mirror comparison+silent normalization+Unicode physical identifier where an ASCII machine alias is required+count-only seal validation+assuming superseded text is active+ignoring exceptions or conflict matrices+repair by overwrite/reset+deleting evidence+changing implementation outside the authorized Codex scope+declaring success with warning, skipped check or unresolved ambiguity\nHistorical names may remain only in explicitly historical records or as compatibility references embedded in provisions issued before the canonical succession. Every such embedded reference automatically resolves through the effective supersession registry directly to one current identity, confers no active authority on the retired identity, and transfers only the responsibility compatible with the successor\'s current boundary; it never transfers retired decision, review, authorization or execution power. Confidential Chinese content remains accessible only to the user and 星澄 while its structural and cryptographic integrity may be checked without disclosure.', E'641bc371434f85baf0a5b358b179ff00cca7cf264f5ab9704c2e4246b52792e0', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D58', E'CODEX_MODULE_DIRECTORY', E'CODEX_DIRECTORY_SPECIAL_LAW', E'codex-directory-closure-certification-and-non-indexing-special-law', E'codex-directory-closure-certification-and-non-indexing-special-law\nAUTHORITY:Codex is the highest normative declaration layer above every sovereign+privileged institution+sub-sovereign+module and is a normalized SQLite Codex, never an ordinary mutable configuration database; DIRECTORY:permission-sovereign exclusively decides directory registration+schema+identity+lifecycle and may not invent domain truth, while domain sovereigns may propose content+evidence but may not self-register; STAR_DIRECTORY:the canonical registered root DIR[DIR_STANDALONE_TOOLS]\\local-model\\model-dialogue\\xingcheng exists and is accepted active with permission-sovereign lifecycle decision+星澄 verification evidence; PENDING-DIRECTORIES:mandated-pending-implementation is an explicit uncovered obligation, never active, and blocks every dependent verified release until complete coverage+tests+acceptance evidence; EPOCH-2-SEAL:remains sealed-read-only-pending-human-governor-signature and only a real offline human-governor signature may close it; EXTERNAL-GATES:external signature and Chinese-mirror confidentiality remain pending until their declared cryptographic+storage+access evidence passes and must never be inferred closed; OBLIGATIONS:all eight implementation obligations remain mandated and due no later than 2026-10-12T15:59:59Z and before the next affected verified release; AMENDMENT:all provision changes are immutable successor records with lineage+canonical hashes+certification+seal and no in-place historical rewrite; NON-INDEXING:the Codex database+Chinese mirror+all Codex content+metadata+structure+hashes+summaries+derivatives are excluded from every RAG+embedding+semantic/vector/full-text/training/search index.; CURRENT-NORMALIZATION:C116 controls;SQLite is retired with zero active consumers;every affirmative SQLite use,fallback,reconciliation,authority or runtime clause in this provision is void and historical-only\nFORBID:treat-Codex-as-config+sovereign-over-Codex+permission-sovereign-invent-domain-truth+domain-self-registration+pending-directory-as-active+fabricated-coverage-evidence+automated-or-inferred-human-signature+premature-external-gate-closure+obligation-waiver-by-runtime+in-place-provision-rewrite+Codex-or-derived-content-in-any-RAG/index/embedding/training corpus+FORBID:SQLite-active-consumer+SQLite-runtime-write+SQLite-fallback+SQLite-reconciliation\nNo machine actor may satisfy the human signature condition. A directory may become active only through a new evidenced acceptance record. 星澄 Chinese-mirror handling remains governed exclusively by the stricter confidential Chinese Codex special law.', E'71ecf61dec099f5743aa6f908b6fd1aca28fd9f194114815f85f3407fe7b5f94', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D59', E'CODEX_MODULE_LANGUAGE', E'CODEX_LANGUAGE_SOURCE_NATIVE_SPECIAL_LAW', E'native-release-push-gate', E'native-release-push-gate\nFLOW:source-revision>changed-scope-classifier>required-native-tests>typed test result contract>C++23-audit>typed audit result contract>Rust/C-contract-evidence>release-gate>Git-coordinator;AUTHORITY:all required evidence current and PASS;PYTHON:none;SCOPE:daily changes run affected plus mandatory governance suites while merge and release run the complete required set;FAILURE:crash+timeout+missing-evidence+schema/runner/version-mismatch returns ERROR|INCOMPLETE|FAIL with receipt.\nFORBID:Python-or-pytest-in-release-push-gate+audit-failure-push+missing-evidence-PASS+stale-result+coverage-reduction+fail-closed-relaxation\nNone.', E'6f6d62f4a4897dffbe456982a0224197cb6498ecb232fd58a11146c776189c25', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D6', E'CODEX_MODULE_ORDINANCE', E'CODEX_SUBORDINATE_ORDINANCES', E'file-extension-conventions', E'file-extension-conventions\nFILE-EXT:per-language-canonical; PYTHON:src=.py/stub=.pyi/test=test_*.py/pkg-init=__init__.py; TYPESCRIPT:logic=.ts/jsx-ui=.tsx/decl=.d.ts/test=.test.ts+.test.tsx; C:impl=.c/interface=.h/test=*_test.c; CPP:impl=.cpp/header=.hpp/template-inline=.inl(when-needed)/test=*_test.cpp; CSHARP:src=.cs/proj=.csproj/solution=.sln/test=*Tests.cs; SQL:general=.sql/migration=.sql; BOUNDARY:C-uses-.h+CPP-uses-.hpp-for-language-edge-visibility; FORBID:inventing-custom-extensions; BASIS:codex+B38-architecture-hybrid\nFORBID:custom-file-extensions; FORBID:cross-language-extension-mismatch; FORBID:mixing-.h-for-cpp-or-.hpp-for-c; FORBID:non-declared-extension\n', E'de349b56183c5005c24ba89bd5568c0c2beb2173585e55a4ee0e2c844b4571ef', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D60', E'CODEX_MODULE_LANGUAGE', E'CODEX_LANGUAGE_SOURCE_NATIVE_SPECIAL_LAW', E'single-c-abi-contract-and-pybind11-purpose-separation-special-law', E'single-c-abi-contract-and-pybind11-purpose-separation-special-law\nBOUNDARY:one registered language-neutral native ABI is the only public native capability boundary;adapters may translate types,errors,lifetimes and calling conventions but own no capability semantics;OWNER:the native implementation owns headers,binding layout and adapter mechanics as owner-local specifications;PROHIBITION:no second public native contract or adapter-owned business logic.\nFORBID:second-public-native-contract+adapter-capability-owner+binding-layout-in-Codex+implementation-file-path-in-Codex\n', E'486c538778c862d154a51936de63cf12743ecb8981b86557f2309cbe76f354a8', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D61', E'CODEX_MODULE_LANGUAGE', E'CODEX_LANGUAGE_SOURCE_NATIVE_SPECIAL_LAW', E'minimal-c-abi-function-budget-and-deferred-capability-table-special-law', E'minimal-c-abi-function-budget-and-deferred-capability-table-special-law\nBOUNDARY:the public native ABI remains minimal and grows only with demonstrated cross-consumer need,compatibility evidence and bounded migration;OWNER:the native implementation owns function count,table layout,symbol structure and admission mechanics as owner-local rules;PROHIBITION:no feature-per-export growth or Codex-fixed function count.\nFORBID:Codex-fixed-function-count+feature-per-export+ABI-growth-without-compatibility-and-consumer-evidence\n', E'adb800eedf33b4447c087469ca3fba731f9d7322b32125211d95b4978786510a', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D62', E'CODEX_MODULE_LANGUAGE', E'CODEX_LANGUAGE_SOURCE_NATIVE_SPECIAL_LAW', E'language-boundary-gate-and-data-only-policy-evidence-only-checker-special-law', E'language-boundary-gate-and-data-only-policy-evidence-only-checker-special-law\nBOUNDARY:language conformance is checked fail-closed against the current language ownership,source-origin,dependency,contract and resource boundaries;OWNER:the language-governance implementation owns triggers,parsers,file extensions,checker layout and evidence encoding as non-authoritative rules;PROHIBITION:checker implementation cannot create authority or modify policy.\nFORBID:checker-file-layout-in-Codex+parser-or-extension-table-as-law+checker-policy-mutation+text-only-verdict\n', E'cc43518b9bb32392457ac0e0d7f40c7e753dd7170086e4436d283dfe670f67c1', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D63', E'CODEX_MODULE_LANGUAGE', E'CODEX_LANGUAGE_SOURCE_NATIVE_SPECIAL_LAW', E'powershell-governance-conflict-and-legacy-infrastructure-evidence-special-law', E'powershell-governance-conflict-and-legacy-infrastructure-evidence-special-law\nSTATUS:PowerShell is not an allowed seventh project language and no general or operational-script exception currently exists; EXISTING:.ps1+.psm1+.psd1 artifacts are classified as GOVERNANCE_CONFLICT and LEGACY_INFRASTRUCTURE_EVIDENCE,not AUTHORED-six-language,GENERATED approval or legal exception; GATE-OUTPUT:LANGUAGE BOUNDARY GATE emits the canonical path+rule=D63+reason=unresolved PowerShell identity governance conflict+evidence_class=legacy infrastructure+execution/use/dependency facts; VERDICT:inventory-only nonexecuting discovery may WARN,while any affected execution+startup+build+install+mutation+integration or release path is FAIL until a successor law resolves identity; EVIDENCE:preserve exact path+hash+owner claim+purpose+callers+commands+inputs/outputs+permissions+side effects+network/process behavior+tests+replacement feasibility without endorsing legality; DECISION-DEFERRED:only an explicit human-governor Codex successor may choose either migration into an approved language or a narrowly defined legal exception; CHECKER:detect+classify+compare+report only and cannot infer necessity,approve usage,create allowlist,grandfather,waive,move,rewrite,delete or repair; MIGRATION/NARROW-EXCEPTION:no action begins before the successor decision and both require separate governed implementation evidence; SUPERSESSION:B70 PowerShell exception declaration is withdrawn and non-operative,while its language-statistics rule for .cpp remains preserved independently by B36+D62.\n\nPACKAGE-AUTO-DEFER:每24小時偵測一次。未具明確新增套件許可者自動標記DEFERRED_AWAITING_PERMISSION；一般新版發布未滿14日者自動標記DEFERRED_OBSERVATION_WINDOW。遞延不等於拒絕、通過或已安裝，遞延期間禁止下載、安裝、鎖定或執行；條件成熟後於下一次週期自動重新評估。重大安全或相容性事件得立即加跑受管檢查。\nFORBID:PowerShell as seventh language+implicit/automatic/legacy exception+checker-created exception or allowlist+continued execution because file already exists+classifying .ps1 as Python/JavaScript-ESM/C/C++/CSharp/SQL+silent ignore+automatic migration/delete/rewrite+WARN used to authorize execution+runtime/build/release bypass+interpreting B70 as current PowerShell authority.\nNone. Even emergency use requires an explicit user command plus a valid Codex successor establishing exact temporary authority; the checker itself can never create that authority.', E'f45c4bd97f3401f696d3e3453600bc096f1181fe05ef0764140f90baf4cadb8a', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D64', E'CODEX_MODULE_LANGUAGE', E'CODEX_LANGUAGE_SOURCE_NATIVE_SPECIAL_LAW', E'semantic-dependency-evidence-and-a205-information-layer-verification', E'semantic-dependency-evidence-and-a205-information-layer-verification\nBOUNDARY:dependency and information-channel evidence must be resolved semantically by the authoritative owner-language and build resolvers;plain text matching cannot establish a verdict;OWNER:resolver choice,parse strategy,graph representation and cache design are owner-local implementation rules;FAILURE:unresolved mandatory edges fail closed.\nFORBID:import-only scan+regex/text-search as final verdict+ignoring dynamic import/include/project/build reference+unresolved alias as absent edge+single build configuration proof+API/IPC accepted because a string mentions information layer+B32 route without registration/contract/authorization/session evidence+direct socket/database/file-drop/private bus hidden behind adapter+stale dependency cache+generated edge without provenance.\n', E'47e556712801f2be0eb853a4f437e597e1ed6c2a5d19528c0fdeeae020826826', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D65', E'CODEX_MODULE_LANGUAGE', E'CODEX_LANGUAGE_SOURCE_NATIVE_SPECIAL_LAW', E'contract-parity-gate', E'contract-parity-gate\nBOUNDARY:every cross-language public contract requires current compatibility,ownership,field,behavior,error,cancellation,deadline and failure evidence;OWNER:checker files,policies,registries and comparison algorithms are owner-local implementation rules;FAILURE:missing or incompatible required evidence denies release.\nFORBID:checker-class/file-layout-in-Codex+implementation-algorithm-as-law+release-on-missing-contract-evidence\n', E'0615670948acb6030832b840d3186ee4bddeb59a866fa8bf743c7fe02a01713b', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D66', E'CODEX_MODULE_LANGUAGE', E'CODEX_LANGUAGE_SOURCE_NATIVE_SPECIAL_LAW', E'native-promotion-gate', E'native-promotion-gate\nQUESTION:does an owner-language capability have sufficient evidence to promote an optimized native executor;FLOW:canonical-owner>reproducible-profile>optimized-executor>versioned-contract-parity>representative-performance+resource evidence>failure+cancellation tests>NATIVE-PROMOTION-GATE;PASS enables the certified path,WARN remains experimental and unreachable from production,FAIL denies activation;REQUIREMENTS:unique owner+measured bottleneck+semantic parity+resource/deadline/cancellation compliance+no duplicate side effect+bounded circuit breaker+owner-native failure disposition;PYTHON:never required as baseline,dispatcher or runtime fallback\nFORBID:production on WARN/FAIL+global fixed speed multiplier+promotion because C++ may be faster+missing owner-language baseline/profile/parity evidence+side effect before safe fallback+retry storm+memory/deadline/cancellation regression+incompatible native artifact+benchmark without representative workload+new feature directly in C++.\nNone except an explicit human-governor successor with impossibility proof under B74.', E'3ca4a18146d9f860614e63a6bafaec4211118e86a41746d91b9a301b09759ccd', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D67', E'CODEX_MODULE_LANGUAGE', E'CODEX_LANGUAGE_SOURCE_NATIVE_SPECIAL_LAW', E'native-promotion-budget-benchmark-evidence-and-lifecycle', E'native-promotion-budget-benchmark-evidence-and-lifecycle\nBOUNDARY:native optimization promotion requires comparable end-to-end correctness,performance,resource,cancellation and failure evidence against the canonical owner path;OWNER:benchmark datasets,metrics,tooling,state names and storage layout are owner-local rules;FAILURE:incomparable or incomplete evidence denies promotion and preserves the last verified path.\nFORBID:fixed universal speedup ratio+compute-only timing+different input/scope/cache/warmup/iterations+missing machine profile+ignored conversion/copy/allocation cost+automatic GIL rule+fallback tested only by missing .pyd+APPROVED without all gates+production EXPERIMENTAL+deleting suspended native code+checker mutation.\n', E'91f4ae66b68c607a5cae790e7dfe947c1b62dd0699971948e518a1ad47c0ae7e', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D68', E'CODEX_MODULE_LANGUAGE', E'CODEX_LANGUAGE_SOURCE_NATIVE_SPECIAL_LAW', E'release-compatibility-evidence-aggregation-and-upgrade-gate', E'release-compatibility-evidence-aggregation-and-upgrade-gate\nGATE:RELEASE_COMPATIBILITY returns exactly PASS|WARN|FAIL and answers:language boundaries intact? API/ABI intact? old consumers work? migrations safely upgrade? native failure falls back? every required gate passed? AGGREGATION:consume immutable evidence only from Language Boundary+Dependency DAG+Contract Parity+Ownership Uniqueness+Native Promotion+Resource and Concurrency+Build ABI Reproducibility Gates; never reimplement their checks; any required FAIL=>release FAIL; WARN blocking is explicit immutable ReleaseCompatibilityPolicy per category and cannot be improvised. STRUCTURE:code/checkers/ReleaseCompatibilityChecker.js+code/policy/ReleaseCompatibilityPolicy.js+code/registry/SupportedVersionRegistry.js+code/evidence/release-compatibility/; policy/registry data only; registry fields release+supported_api_range+supported_abi_range+supported_schema_range+supported_previous_releases. MATRIX:compare current release with every previous supported release for JavaScript/CSharp API,CSharp/native parity+FSharp domain parity,C ABI major/minor+symbols,CSharp/native interop,SQL schema+migration,current Codex principle,permission and typed-contract entry,native artifact architecture/runtime/toolchain; prove prior API/ABI ranges and schema upgrade path remain supported. CHANGE-CLASS:PATCH permits bug fix/internal optimization/performance/implementation only and denies contract/ABI/schema break;MINOR permits optional field,new operation/capability/ABI symbol only while old consumer works;MAJOR alone permits removal/required rename/operation or ABI symbol removal/layout/incompatible semantics with explicit migration. CONSUMERS:test old JavaScript client>new CSharp backend and new client>supported old backend when bidirectional window declared; old supported native consumer>new C ABI load+behavior. SQL-UPGRADE:old schema>ordered transactional migration>new schema>new application; verify rollback policy+data preservation+indexes+constraints and activation order before CSharp requires new field. NATIVE-DUAL:every approved fallback path is exercised under the same compatibility window.\n\nPACKAGE-AUTO-DEFER:每24小時偵測一次。未具明確新增套件許可者自動標記DEFERRED_AWAITING_PERMISSION；一般新版發布未滿14日者自動標記DEFERRED_OBSERVATION_WINDOW。遞延不等於拒絕、通過或已安裝，遞延期間禁止下載、安裝、鎖定或執行；條件成熟後於下一次週期自動重新評估。重大安全或相容性事件得立即加跑受管檢查。\nFORBID:new-new pair only+required gate FAIL overridden+WARN policy invented at runtime+PATCH contract/ABI/schema change+MINOR breaking old consumer+major break without migration+SQL migration execution-only test+new field used before migration+native-only integration test+fallback failure accepted+missing N-1 upgrade+incomplete manifest+automatic major bump+contract/ABI/migration/fallback mutation+lowered standard+self-repair.\nA project declaring no backward compatibility window must still test N-1 migration to a typed unsupported-version outcome that preserves data and supports rollback; silent breakage is never allowed.', E'67b77badae0186b25f9caa804144b07f3b9c9e0cb3d003d7821fb85f7a105f2b', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D69', E'CODEX_MODULE_LANGUAGE', E'CODEX_LANGUAGE_SOURCE_NATIVE_SPECIAL_LAW', E'language-governance-final-decision-and-evidence-freshness-gate', E'language-governance-final-decision-and-evidence-freshness-gate\nBOUNDARY:the language governance gate produces one acceptance result from current required evidence and fails closed on critical violations or missing proof;OWNER:gate ordering,change-scope planning,record layout,checker files and evidence reuse algorithms are owner-local implementation rules;PROHIBITION:checkers cannot grant waivers,change policy or treat missing evidence as success.\nFORBID:gate-file-layout-in-Codex+implementation-record-schema-as-law+checker-created-waiver+missing-evidence-as-pass\n', E'5d15debe57d9f3573d870eb295ee1c64f916cfa8b503510b32f54a1b9225e00b', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D7', E'CODEX_MODULE_ORDINANCE', E'CODEX_SUBORDINATE_ORDINANCES', E'test-framework-final-ownership', E'test-framework-final-ownership\nTEST-TIER:unit-by-implementation-language+cross-language-integration-under-CSharp-TestSuiteOrchestrator;UNIT:C/C++=native-harness|Rust=cargo-test|Go=go-test|CSharp/FSharp=dotnet-test|JavaScript-ESM=Rust-hosted-browser-contract-harness|Julia=Julia-native-test|PostgreSQL=migration-replay;INTEGRATION:CSharp-TestSuiteOrchestrator is sole orchestrator and emits typed test result contract;PYTHON:none;TRAINING:JAX training artifacts are validated by native contract and model-evaluation suites without Python test ownership.\nFORBID:second-test-orchestrator+Python-test+pytest+cross-language-unit-framework-mixing+skip-required-integration-tier\nNone.', E'29ebb6cb5a0b465cc5c07f9296a7fc1c62f61ff8acc28af518a330c5cd53ad5c', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D70', E'CODEX_MODULE_LANGUAGE', E'CODEX_LANGUAGE_SOURCE_NATIVE_SPECIAL_LAW', E'unified-language-source-index-graph-ir-and-incremental-planner', E'unified-language-source-index-graph-ir-and-incremental-planner\nBOUNDARY:language analysis uses one current source index and dependency graph generation shared by all applicable governance checks;OWNER:parser set,intermediate representation,node and edge forms,cache keys and incremental algorithms are owner-local implementation rules;PROHIBITION:no checker-private authority graph or stale generation reuse.\nFORBID:parser-list-or-IR-layout-in-Codex+checker-private-index+stale-generation+partial-graph-publication\n', E'04db090e34e8581e53fc62055e321536338df1ec16bb535f7938df4b80dc1fd1', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D71', E'CODEX_MODULE_LANGUAGE', E'CODEX_LANGUAGE_SOURCE_NATIVE_SPECIAL_LAW', E'governance-full-scan-baseline-incremental-golden-parity-and-cache-correctness', E'governance-full-scan-baseline-incremental-golden-parity-and-cache-correctness\nBOUNDARY:incremental governance optimization must remain verdict-equivalent to a reproducible complete analysis and must invalidate every affected dependency on source,policy,contract or toolchain change;OWNER:benchmark scenarios,measurements,golden datasets,cache format and thresholds are owner-local rules;FAILURE:any mismatch falls back to complete analysis or denies the gate.\nFORBID:benchmark-scenario-list-in-Codex+implementation-threshold-as-law+incremental-verdict-drift+stale-cache-acceptance\n', E'9f7febc281b55b686775b290cd2e3827bfb603a45c4c552cc49dd531f001263e', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D72', E'CODEX_MODULE_LANGUAGE', E'CODEX_LANGUAGE_SOURCE_NATIVE_SPECIAL_LAW', E'language-governance-schema-current-role-freeze', E'language-governance-schema-current-role-freeze\nPURPOSE:freeze-current-language-ownership-without-freezing-feature-development;CURRENT-ROLE-MAP:B35;CURRENT-BOUNDARIES:B37+B38+B50;PUBLIC-CONTRACT:versioned-request+response+event+error+cancellation+deadline;EVOLUTION:role-or-boundary-change-requires-new-version+compatibility+owner-migration+consumer-update+retirement;INTERNAL:parser+cache+graph+adapter implementations replaceable when semantics stay equivalent;PERFORMANCE:governed by B157+D35\nFORBID:restore-retired-role-map+Python-control-or-business-owner+unversioned-boundary-change+duplicate-owner+public-consumer-on-private-internal-type+experimental-checker-as-authority\n', E'e962936c2463fcbfba50382bb237e4a9447e9cc54faf0c0704ed2fddeecbb6bb', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D73', E'CODEX_MODULE_FOUNDATION', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'whole-codex-normative-surface-precedence-and-delegation-closure', E'whole-codex-normative-surface-precedence-and-delegation-closure\nINTEGRATION:Codex is the single highest normative declaration layer and not an application runtime;SURFACE:only principles+articles+edicts+responsibilities+authority+prohibitions+cross-layer invariants;EXCLUDED:business rules+implementation specifications+module algorithms+internal workflows+operational parameters+UI details+test implementation;DELEGATION:B164+B165 place excluded content under each owning implementation layer as non-authoritative versioned rules;PRECEDENCE:current Codex boundary controls conflicts while implementation rule controls only its declared owner-local behavior;CROSS-LAYER:shared behavior requires one registered versioned contract with one semantic owner;LIFECYCLE:every Codex provision and delegated implementation rule keeps separate identity+lineage+version+status and may never be silently promoted across layers;PROJECTION:directories+indexes+mirrors+architecture documents+evidence only explain+validate+accelerate and cannot create authority;AUTO-CLASSIFICATION:every new or changed requirement is classified before storage;CODEX-CLASS:principle+article+edict+responsibility+authority-boundary+permission/security/canonical-data-boundary+prohibition+cross-layer-invariant+shared-contract-ownership;IMPLEMENTATION-CLASS:business-rule+domain-validation+algorithm+parameter+internal-workflow+query+retry+batch+cache+format/codec/layout+UI-behavior+test-implementation+operational-tunable;MIXED-CLASS:split into minimum Codex invariant and owner-local implementation rule joined by controlling_provision+contract_identity;DECISION-ORDER:authority/security/permission/canonicality/cross-owner-effect first>cross-layer contract second>owner-local behavior third;DEFAULT:owner-local behavior is implementation-derived-non-authoritative;AMBIGUITY:if a requirement can grant power+change authority+cross owner or weaken a prohibition classify its boundary as Codex and defer only the unresolved implementation detail;OUTPUT:classification+owner+scope+reason+controlling_provision+target_registry+source_revision+status;NO-DUPLICATION:one semantic rule has one owner and one authoritative location;VERSION-AUTHORITY:LATEST-PUBLISHED-ONLY;CURRENT:exactly one codex_version equals current_version and active binding version and alone has authority_status=CURRENT_AUTHORITATIVE;HISTORY:every earlier version is immutable+non-authoritative and labeled HISTORICAL_SUPERSEDED;LABEL:version_identity+authority_status+successor_version+retired_at+reason+immutable;TRANSITION:publishing a newer version atomically demotes the prior current version and every prior generation remains historical;READ:historical versions may be queried only for lineage+audit+comparison+recovery evidence and every response carries the historical label;CACHE/REPLICA:never restores authority;ROLLBACK:must publish a new later successor version and never reactivate an old identity;CONFLICT:only latest current version may decide or bind;LITERAL-POLICY:mutable path+port+tool/model/package version+deadline+resource limit+threshold+batch/cache/retry value is referenced by canonical directory/parameter/contract code;explicit literals remain only for immutable identity grammar+cryptographic/interoperability constant+closed enum+safety invariant;FILE-PROTECTION:filesystem-read-only is a narrow projection-integrity aid and never authority;READONLY-REQUIRED:only current generated confidential Chinese mirror parts;WRITABLE-GOVERNED:architecture projections+package marker+renderer inputs+all non-mirror Codex workspace files remain writable through normal permission+version+audit controls;AUTHORITY:PostgreSQL Codex permissions+transaction+version+current-binding+seal govern official mutation;PUBLICATION:renderer may temporarily unlock mirror targets and must restore read-only after verified atomic generation;DRIFT:content/version mismatch fails closed regardless of file attribute;MINIMIZATION:no file is read-only merely because it is located in the Codex directory\nFORBID:Codex-as-business-rule-store+Codex-as-implementation-manual+implementation-rule-as-law+parallel-authority+implicit-precedence+derived-projection-writing-law+historical-rule-current+pending-as-active+cross-layer-contract-without-owner+mirror-divergence;FORBID:unclassified-rule+same-rule-in-Codex-and-implementation-registry+implementation-detail-promoted-to-Codex-by-convenience+authority-boundary-hidden-as-business-rule+mixed-requirement-stored-unsplit;FORBID:two-authoritative-versions+old-version-as-current+unlabeled-history+historical-write-or-adjudication+cache/replica/restore-promoting-old-version+rollback-reactivating-old-identity+current-binding-version-mismatch;FORBID:mutable-operational-literal-in-Codex-article+duplicated-parameter-value+deployment-setting-as-normative-law;FORBID:directory-wide-read-only+read-only-as-authority+architecture-projection-read-only-without-necessity+read-only-blocking-governed-sync+mirror-left-writable-after-publication;FORBID:directory-wide-read-only+read-only-as-authority+architecture-projection-read-only-without-necessity+read-only-blocking-governed-sync+mirror-left-writable-after-publication\nOwner-local implementation rules remain constrained by current Codex authority, security, permission, resource and cross-layer contract boundaries.', E'f0258e596dee0969384c880f089671f65399107a9daaf017e8650c4bd6fe52b4', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D74', E'CODEX_MODULE_DIRECTORY', E'CODEX_DIRECTORY_SPECIAL_LAW', E'codex-directory-closure-certification-and-non-indexing-clean-successor', E'codex-directory-closure-certification-and-non-indexing-clean-successor\nAUTHORITY:Codex is the highest normative declaration layer above every sovereign,privileged institution,sub-sovereign and module and is a normalized SQLite Codex,never ordinary mutable configuration;it is not an active sovereign. DIRECTORY:permission-sovereign exclusively decides directory registration,schema,identity,access and lifecycle and cannot invent domain truth;domain owners propose truth/evidence and cannot self-register. STAR-DIRECTORY:the registered Xingcheng root remains a distinct confidential identity even when physically nested under a local-model boundary;physical nesting never merges XINGCHENG with MODEL_DIALOGUE. Activation requires permission lifecycle decision plus verified filesystem,ownership,format,coverage and confidentiality evidence. PENDING:mandated-pending-implementation is an uncovered obligation,never active,and blocks every dependent verified release until complete tests and acceptance evidence. SEALS:Epoch 2 remains sealed-read-only-pending-human-governor-signature;only a real offline human-governor signature closes it. External signature and Chinese-Codex confidentiality gates remain pending until cryptographic,storage and access evidence passes and are never inferred closed. OBLIGATIONS:declared implementation obligations remain binding through their recorded deadlines and affected release gates;runtime cannot waive them. AMENDMENT:provision changes use immutable successors,lineage,canonical hashes,certification and seals;historical content is not rewritten. NON-INDEXING:Codex database,confidential Chinese Codex and all Codex content,metadata,structure,hashes,summaries and derivatives are excluded from RAG,embedding,semantic/vector/full-text,training and search indexes. CONFIDENTIALITY:Chinese Codex handling is governed only by its stricter confidential special law and may be viewed by 星澄 solely within its authorized protected boundary.; CURRENT-NORMALIZATION:C116 controls;SQLite is retired with zero active consumers;every affirmative SQLite use,fallback,reconciliation,authority or runtime clause in this provision is void and historical-only\nFORBID:Codex as config or active sovereign+permission owner inventing domain truth+domain self-registration+pending treated active+fabricated evidence/signature+runtime obligation waiver+historical in-place rewrite+Codex content indexed/trained+XINGCHENG/MODEL_DIALOGUE identity merger+Chinese Codex reference,mirror,export or disclosure outside authorized 星澄 boundary.+FORBID:SQLite-active-consumer+SQLite-runtime-write+SQLite-fallback+SQLite-reconciliation\nCertified tooling may read the official machine Codex through the governed repository interface without direct mutation authority. No machine actor may satisfy the human signature condition.', E'46ed38bbfc2c45e3864c853e532ff223db0723d251401aea04deb47e678f5ea1', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D75', E'CODEX_MODULE_ORDINANCE', E'CODEX_SUBORDINATE_ORDINANCES', E'non-disruptive-codex-amendment-ordinance-flow', E'non-disruptive-codex-amendment-ordinance-flow\nPURPOSE:a Codex amendment must not interrupt,stop,restart,disconnect,reconfigure or partially mutate the running system. Every amendment follows this ordinance flow:1 RECEIVE explicit human/user amendment command and immutable amendment_id;2 SNAPSHOT current active Codex generation,history head,seals,read-only attributes and runtime reader generation;3 STAGE all proposed rows and Chinese confidential representation in an isolated non-authoritative transaction/generation;4 NORMALIZE identity,law classification,lineage,lifecycle,effective records,directories,test flows,metadata and version 1.00000 evolution rules;5 VALIDATE SQLite integrity,foreign keys,history/hash chain,seal roots,known references,unique scoped successors,authority/lifecycle/effective parity,confidentiality,mirror parity and applicable tests/audit;6 CERTIFY required evidence without fabricating external or human signatures;7 PREPARE immutable successor and generation manifest with rollback pointer to prior snapshot;8 ATOMIC-PUBLISH the complete generation by one generation-fenced pointer/transaction;9 NOTIFY consumers through typed shared-layer contract;10 RELOAD policy views only at safe boundaries using snapshot isolation;11 VERIFY old in-flight readers finish on prior generation,new readers use the published generation,system health/channel continuity remain intact;12 AUDIT result and restore read-only protection. Runtime services continue with the last fully accepted generation throughout staging/validation. No service may observe half-written Codex state. Publication does not itself execute newly declared implementation obligations,repair/update code,change permissions or restart a backend;those proceed through their own authorized ordinance and user-confirmation gates. If any step fails,the staged generation is rejected/quarantined,the active pointer remains unchanged,running service continues,and evidence is emitted. Concurrent amendments serialize by amendment lock and rebase/revalidate against the actual current history head;no lost update. Consumer incompatibility yields INCOMPLETE_EVIDENCE or rejection,never forced reload. Emergency rollback is pointer restoration only to a previously sealed accepted generation and cannot erase the failed attempt or history.; CURRENT-NORMALIZATION:C116 controls;SQLite is retired with zero active consumers;every affirmative SQLite use,fallback,reconciliation,authority or runtime clause in this provision is void and historical-only\nFORBID:editing active generation in place+partial table/mirror publication+runtime restart or channel disconnect caused only by Codex update+new rule auto-executing implementation+publication before validation+fabricated signature+reader seeing mixed generations+concurrent lost amendment+failed staging replacing active snapshot+rollback by reset/overwrite/history deletion+Codex watcher triggering recursive repair/update.+FORBID:SQLite-active-consumer+SQLite-runtime-write+SQLite-fallback+SQLite-reconciliation\nA new rule may explicitly require a later controlled system restart for its own implementation, but the Codex amendment transaction itself remains non-disruptive and only records that pending obligation. A security-critical rule may block new unsafe operations after atomic publication while existing safe in-flight operations drain.', E'a0f1c884769061cf4a6210f412ddf6552278840d173addacadd907b6ea755dd0', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D76', E'CODEX_MODULE_ORDINANCE', E'CODEX_SUBORDINATE_ORDINANCES', E'codex-readonly-state-review-isolation', E'codex-readonly-state-review-isolation\nCodex filesystem read-only state is a Codex protection control,not a prerequisite for inspecting or auditing unrelated system/runtime/module health. If a Codex artifact is unexpectedly writable,the reviewer records CODEX_PROTECTION_DEGRADED,verifies content hash/history/seal and isolates Codex mutation/publication;the condition does not stop,fail,skip or contaminate independent system review and does not make the running system unhealthy by itself. System review must continue and report its own findings. Writable state never grants amendment authority and never makes changed content effective. After an authorized amendment transaction,read-only protection is restored and separately verified. If content integrity also changed without authority,the last sealed generation remains authoritative while the incident is isolated and audited;unaffected runtime continues.\nFORBID:using writable attribute alone to abort unrelated system review+reporting whole system failed solely because Codex is writable+trusting writable content as effective+silently ignoring writable state+automatic reset/overwrite to repair attributes+mixing Codex-protection finding into unrelated module verdict.\nA review specifically scoped to Codex protection may fail or block Codex publication on writable state;that scoped verdict still cannot replace the independent system review result.', E'cba43d01774cd5353e3ae21752acc398755de8aa9fb77a47009efde92482dee0', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D77', E'CODEX_MODULE_FOUNDATION', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'dynamic-test-management-roster-and-closure-status-successor', E'dynamic-test-management-roster-and-closure-status-successor\nTEST-OWNERSHIP:owner=permission-sovereign in test_flow_directory and test_suite_architecture_directory means directory identity,schema,access and lifecycle authority only. health-maintenance-test-sub-sovereign is centralized management_owner for one-module-one-suite inventory,planning,scheduling,fixtures,execution coordination,evidence collection,retest and status reporting;it has no policy decision or direct module execution power and dispatches governed module test executors. A test flow without a physical management_owner field resolves it through its suite/module registry and this provision;unresolved mapping is incomplete evidence. Domain owners define expected domain truth/evidence but cannot self-register or suppress results. TEST-ACTIVATION:test suite status mandated means required but not proven active. A suite becomes active only through module path existence,ownership,language-appropriate unit tests,pytest integration when applicable,fixtures,isolation,cleanup,current passing evidence and maintenance-manager acceptance. Counts are always computed from current registries and never frozen into rules. ROSTERS:top current institution roster and active sub-sovereign roster are separate registry-derived views. TOP={decision-sovereign,system-runtime-sovereign,automation-sovereign,permission-sovereign,星澄};Codex is excluded. SUB is exactly the active children in sovereign_hierarchy_registry whose lineage/lifecycle/effective state and parent are consistent. Displaying a generic active lineage query as the top roster is forbidden. HISTORICAL-CORRECTION:H045 damaged display token is corrected by immutable annotation to confidential 星澄 audit;original history bytes,entry_hash,sequence and authority remain unchanged. Consumers display the annotation with raw evidence. DYNAMIC-PENDING:directory implementation,all test suites,external signatures,Epoch human signature and Language Governance lifecycle are read live from their canonical registries. pending/mandated/signature-required/FREEZE-PENDING remains a real blocker until its own acceptance evidence and immutable transition record pass. A count,report date or prior audit cannot be used as permanent current state. STATUS-SNAPSHOT:reports may state counts only with source revision,registry hash,generated_at and stale-after;after expiry or registry change they are observations,not rules.\nFORBID:permission owner treated as test manager+maintenance manager making policy/permission decisions+mandated suite treated active+hard-coded pending/test/signature counts as permanent truth+top roster mixed with children+Codex in active roster+alias as canonical ID+rewriting H045+annotation changing history hash+stale status snapshot closing a gate+pending state closed without evidence.\nA module may execute its own unit tests under centralized management without receiving suite ownership. A timestamped report may include exact current counts when clearly labeled derived evidence with revision,hash and expiry.', E'260c58d17b40d142d3c8556a9004a61ac27d2e016b43f35f83f4661568c14e33', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D78', E'CODEX_MODULE_FOUNDATION', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'timestamp-only-hardcoding-invariant', E'timestamp-only-hardcoding-invariant\nONLY-HARDCODE-ALLOWANCE:the only literal runtime/deployment value permitted to be hardcoded is a timestamp value created for an immutable event,revision,evidence or audit record. Every other value without exception is referenced through CODE[identifier].field or a registered governed environment variable under C68-A107. Paths,roots,filenames,ports,endpoints,hosts,branches,remotes,model names,dimensions,chunk sizes,collection/database/table names,language lists,state values,versions,IDs,owners,roles,timeouts,retries,budgets,limits,thresholds,feature flags and defaults cannot be duplicated as hardcoded literals in current law or implementation. Their single defining values live in typed canonical registries;even fixed legal enums and version identities receive codes and consumers reference the code. TIMESTAMP:hardcoded timestamp must be generated by the authoritative clock at event time,include timezone/UTC semantics and precision,be immutable after record creation and never be reused as configuration,deadline,timeout or identity. Historical literals remain immutable evidence but must be mapped to codes and cannot be copied forward. Source/checker scans classify authored literals,resolve exemptions only for typed timestamp fields and emit FAIL for every other hardcoded operational value.\nFORBID:any non-timestamp hardcoded value+claiming a value fixed to evade code registration+timestamp used as configuration/default/timeout+manual fabricated event time+historical literal copied into successor+checker inventing literal whitelist+generated code hiding authored hardcode.\nTest fixtures may contain isolated synthetic values only as fixture data declared by a registered fixture code;source still references the fixture code. Third-party/generated artifacts are evidence-classified and cannot supply authoritative configuration.', E'524468d33c418e6ebdedcaa6adc7b230a5a9e7838846e354de68a40b5feeefe9', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D79', E'CODEX_MODULE_FOUNDATION', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'canonical-timestamp-envelope-fields', E'canonical-timestamp-envelope-fields\nTIMESTAMP-ENVELOPE:every immutable event/evidence/audit/revision record uses the applicable formal fields occurred_at_utc,recorded_at_utc,observed_at_utc,effective_at_utc,expires_at_utc,source_clock_id,time_zone,utc_offset,precision,monotonic_sequence,clock_skew_ms,timestamp_status and timestamp_hash. occurred_at_utc is when the source event happened;recorded_at_utc is durable append time;observed_at_utc is measurement time;effective_at_utc is legal/config activation time;expires_at_utc is nullable only when non-expiry is legally declared. FIXED-FORMAT:every canonical UTC timestamp is exactly YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss.ffffffZ in Gregorian calendar,24-hour time,UTC,with six fractional-second digits and uppercase Z;canonical storage forbids omitted fractions,numeric offsets,spaces,locale month names and naive time. precision is fixed to microsecond. time_zone and utc_offset are separate display/source-evidence fields and never alter canonical UTC storage. source_clock_id references the registered clock;monotonic_sequence orders events when wall clock ties/regresses;clock_skew_ms records measured uncertainty;timestamp_status is verified|estimated|corrected|invalid;timestamp_hash binds the normalized envelope to its record. HARD-CODE:only concrete immutable values stored in these timestamp fields qualify for D78 allowance. Field names,format,zones,clock IDs,expiry policy and status vocabulary are referenced by schema codes rather than scattered literals. CORRECTION:timestamps are never overwritten;an error appends a corrected successor with original timestamp_hash,reason,authority and correlation_id. VALIDATION:permission-sovereign formally validates time evidence as part of audit validation;domain collectors supply source evidence. Missing required field,wrong fixed format,naive local time,impossible ordering,excess skew,unregistered clock or hash mismatch makes evidence incomplete/invalid without stopping unrelated system review.\nFORBID:canonical timestamp outside YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss.ffffffZ+ambiguous local time+missing required source zone evidence+recorded time substituted for occurrence without status+timestamp overwrite+clock regression hidden+timestamp literal outside formal field+timestamp used as configuration identity+unregistered clock+permission validator fabricating source time+invalid time failing unrelated system review.\nLegacy records may retain their original format when paired with a canonical converted UTC timestamp and immutable migration evidence;the original is evidence only. A source unable to prove occurrence time uses estimated status and explicit uncertainty;it cannot claim verified.', E'8c2c1dd54a31d675a1114a3e6abe1a966264fe711916cd18f8f29f5adc018fcc', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D8', E'CODEX_MODULE_AUTHORITY', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'self-health-test-necessity', E'self-health-test-necessity\nSELF-HEALTH-TEST:necessary-for-self-maintenance-health; OWNER:health-maintenance-test-sub-sovereign; SCOPE:governed-tools-declare-test-files; REQUIRE:collectable-offline+no-live-model-dependency; DETECT:governance-audit-collects-managed-test-files; BASIS:codex+D7-test-framework-tiering\n\nPACKAGE-AUTO-DEFER:每24小時偵測一次。未具明確新增套件許可者自動標記DEFERRED_AWAITING_PERMISSION；一般新版發布未滿14日者自動標記DEFERRED_OBSERVATION_WINDOW。遞延不等於拒絕、通過或已安裝，遞延期間禁止下載、安裝、鎖定或執行；條件成熟後於下一次週期自動重新評估。重大安全或相容性事件得立即加跑受管檢查。\nFORBID:delete-required-test-file; FORBID:test-depends-on-live-model/network; FORBID:uncollectable-test-file\n', E'69aee6e7acdf3f0a46bbdc027e5bb006e025dfe483c7f58b1acb9fe220ac47de', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D80', E'CODEX_MODULE_XINGCHENG', E'CODEX_STAR_PRIVILEGED_INSTITUTION_SPECIAL_LAW', E'xingcheng-codex-implementation-compliance-classification', E'xingcheng-codex-implementation-compliance-classification\nMANDATE:CODE[INSTITUTION_XINGCHENG] inspects not only runtime faults but also whether CODE[CODEX_CURRENT_GENERATION] and governed implementation agree. Inspection scope includes declarations,authority/ownership,paths through directory codes,identities,contracts,API/ABI/schema,dependency direction,configuration codes,environment bindings,security,tests,evidence,lifecycle,release state and observable runtime behavior. INPUTS:use the current sealed/effective Codex generation,canonical registries,SourceIndex/GovernanceIR/LanguageGraph,current source/build/runtime evidence and affected-scope/full verification as applicable. Never compare against a stale report or superseded provision. METHOD:1 resolve current applicable provisions and codes;2 state the expected obligation and acceptance evidence;3 collect implementation declaration plus observed evidence;4 test contradiction,absence,ambiguity and feasibility;5 trace ownership and revision;6 classify;7 issue separate findings;8 submit audit evidence to CODE[ROLE_PERMISSION_SOVEREIGN] for formal validation. CLASSIFICATION:CODE[FINDING_IMPLEMENTATION_ISSUE] applies only when the Codex rule is current,internally coherent,applicable and testable but source/config/build/runtime/evidence violates or omits it. CODE[FINDING_CODEX_ISSUE] applies only when the governing rule itself is contradictory,ambiguous,missing required semantics,uses unresolved/duplicate codes,has invalid lineage/lifecycle/precedence,requires impossible evidence or conflicts with a higher/current provision. CODE[FINDING_INCOMPLETE_EVIDENCE] applies when neither conclusion is provable;it cannot be reported as compliant. If one incident contains both,a single vague BOTH verdict is forbidden:emit two linked findings,one implementation issue and one Codex issue,each with its own evidence,owner and required action. OUTPUT:each finding includes finding_id,classification,rule/code references,implementation target,expected,observed,evidence hashes,source revision,CodeX generation,scope,severity,certainty,owner,impact,required action,retest condition,correlation_id and CODE[TIMESTAMP_FORMAT_CANONICAL] timestamps. ROUTING:implementation issue goes to its registered implementation owner and normal repair/change workflow;Codex issue goes to explicit user/human amendment workflow under CODE[CODEX_AMENDMENT_FLOW],never automatic source repair. CODE[INSTITUTION_XINGCHENG] may challenge,suggest and re-inspect but cannot formally validate its own audit evidence,change permission or silently amend Codex. EFFECT:no finding alone mutates code,Codex,registry or status. Critical mismatch isolates only unsafe affected scope;unaffected system review and runtime continue.\n\nPACKAGE-AUTO-DEFER:每24小時偵測一次。未具明確新增套件許可者自動標記DEFERRED_AWAITING_PERMISSION；一般新版發布未滿14日者自動標記DEFERRED_OBSERVATION_WINDOW。遞延不等於拒絕、通過或已安裝，遞延期間禁止下載、安裝、鎖定或執行；條件成熟後於下一次週期自動重新評估。重大安全或相容性事件得立即加跑受管檢查。\nFORBID:fault-only inspection+assuming implementation wrong whenever mismatch exists+assuming Codex wrong to excuse implementation+vague combined verdict+classification without current rule and observed evidence+stale/superseded comparison+automatic Codex rewrite+CODE[INSTITUTION_XINGCHENG] self-validating formal audit+finding directly executing repair+missing owner/retest/correlation+compliance PASS on incomplete evidence.\nA fast save-time inspection may use affected-scope evidence and mark untouched scopes not-evaluated;integration/release or Codex-wide claims require full applicable verification. Emergency isolation may precede final classification but cannot predetermine it.', E'c2a8373fa98d92d7d70c9e152471d37b4fc8f3c4887ac16f4cb587863fe002ce', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D81', E'CODEX_MODULE_XINGCHENG', E'CODEX_STAR_PRIVILEGED_INSTITUTION_SPECIAL_LAW', E'precise-coded-fault-and-compliance-detail-display', E'precise-coded-fault-and-compliance-detail-display\nNO-VAGUE-FINDING:every fault,implementation issue and Codex issue is displayed as a concrete individually addressable record;generic labels such as system error,unknown failure,compliance problem or something went wrong cannot be the final finding. IDENTITY:display CODE[FAULT_CODE] or CODE[COMPLIANCE_FINDING_CODE] plus CODE[CANONICAL_CODENAME],human title and classification. DETAIL:the required governed detail schema contains finding_id,incident_id,parent/root_cause_group,classification_code,fault_or_rule_code,canonical_codename,title,summary,full_detail,severity,certainty,status,source_revision,CodeX_generation,affected_module_code,owner_code,exact_file_code,resolved_file_path,repository_root_code,line_start,line_end,symbol_or_entry,artifact_or_process,contract_or_operation,rule/provision references,expected,observed,reproduction_or_detection_steps,root_cause,impact,affected_scope,isolation_state,proposed_action_code,action_detail,risk,rollback_or_fallback,retest_condition,evidence hashes,correlation_id and formal timestamps. FILE-PRECISION:implementation findings must resolve to the narrowest authored source/config/build/migration/test file responsible and include line range plus symbol/entry when parse evidence permits. Multiple responsible files are separate linked targets,not one directory-level accusation. Runtime/generated artifact faults identify the artifact/process and trace to its owning authored file or explicitly state which mapping evidence is missing under CODE[FINDING_INCOMPLETE_EVIDENCE]. Codex issues identify exact provision_id/table/row/field or missing provision slot and the conflicting higher/current rule;CODEX database filename alone is insufficient. DISPLAY:single fault shows one full record;multiple faults show every record separately in deterministic severity,time,code order with total/unresolved counts. Collapsed summaries may accompany but never replace details. Paths are rendered from CODE[DIRECTORY_REFERENCE].field and are derived display values,not new hardcoding. REDACTION:secrets/personal/confidential Codex content is redacted by field policy while preserving code,location class,hash and actionable reason;redaction cannot make the finding vague. VALIDATION:CODE[ROLE_PERMISSION_SOVEREIGN] rejects any audit finding lacking required identity,exact target,expected/observed,evidence or retest fields.\nFORBID:vague final error+missing code or codename+directory-only implementation target when file is knowable+missing line/symbol without parser reason+multiple files/faults collapsed into one target+Codex issue without exact provision/table/field+details replaced by summary+unknown used without enumerating missing evidence+hardcoded path instead of directory code+redaction hiding actionable classification+formal validation of incomplete detail.\nWhen a crash prevents immediate file resolution,the preliminary record may use CODE[FINDING_INCOMPLETE_EVIDENCE] with exact artifact/process,stack/evidence and missing mapping;it must be enriched before repair approval or final classification. Line numbers may be omitted for binary artifacts when symbol/build/source mapping is provided.', E'af23929bcf2f53b67b0503a436e2f99fd20c45edded7d7b0b0f549614f42ab48', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D82', E'CODEX_MODULE_FOUNDATION', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'code-reference-and-hardcoding-separation-successor', E'code-reference-and-hardcoding-separation-successor\nSUCCESSOR:D78 is superseded. GENERAL-RULE:operational values are resolved from typed canonical code registries or governed environment bindings and are not duplicated across law or implementation. SEPARATION:this article governs only literal/reference placement;it does not define timestamp representation or version-number semantics. Timestamp fields,format,clock evidence and correction are governed exclusively by D79. Version namespaces,format,authority,evolution and comparison are governed exclusively by D83 together with their cited version provisions. A timestamp value and a version number are distinct typed identities and neither may substitute for,derive from,or encode the other. DEFINITION:authoritative registry declarations,legal schema definitions,code identities and immutable evidence values are canonical definitions rather than duplicated operational hardcoding;their consumers still reference registered identities. CHECKING:a finding must name the literal,its semantic class,the expected registry/environment/timestamp/version authority and the exact file or Codex field.\nFORBID:combining timestamp-format and version-format into one rule+timestamp used as version+version used as time+duplicated operational literal+checker treating canonical registry definition as consumer hardcoding+checker inventing exemptions+copying historical literal into a new operational consumer.\nTest fixtures may use registered synthetic fixture data. Third-party/generated artifacts remain classified evidence and cannot become configuration authority.', E'bb6d31ffafc514ddf8c0e82ddabad01acb4e14c56ecfb4f2d1d17cf81d10cb3f', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D83', E'CODEX_MODULE_FOUNDATION', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'canonical-version-number-contract', E'canonical-version-number-contract\nVERSION-ONLY:this article governs version numbers and never timestamp fields or clock evidence. NAMESPACES:Codex version,application version,tool version,release identity,contract version,schema version,ABI version,governance-schema version and runtime generation are typed non-interchangeable identities with one registered authority each. CODEX-FORMAT:the current Epoch 2 Codex version is the exact five-fractional-digit decimal identity 1.00000 until an explicit user amendment authorizes natural evolution;revision history may advance while this version remains unchanged. EVOLUTION:version changes follow the registered version-evolution policy and immutable successor history;automatic repair,automatic update,models,checkers and runtime processes cannot infer,bump,normalize,downgrade or rewrite a version. COMPARISON:compare only within the same namespace using its registered parser and authority;floating-point arithmetic,filesystem time,Git time,build time and event timestamps are never version authority. DISPLAY:a timestamp may accompany a version record only as separate metadata and cannot be embedded into or parsed as the version number.\n\nPACKAGE-AUTO-DEFER:每24小時偵測一次。未具明確新增套件許可者自動標記DEFERRED_AWAITING_PERMISSION；一般新版發布未滿14日者自動標記DEFERRED_OBSERVATION_WINDOW。遞延不等於拒絕、通過或已安裝，遞延期間禁止下載、安裝、鎖定或執行；條件成熟後於下一次週期自動重新評估。重大安全或相容性事件得立即加跑受管檢查。\nFORBID:timestamp-derived version+version-derived timestamp+date-version substitution+cross-namespace comparison+floating-point version arithmetic+automatic bump/reset/downgrade+filename/path/mtime/Git/package/cache as version authority+silent normalization+combining version and timestamp fields.\nA legacy externally defined semantic version may retain its native registered syntax inside its own namespace;it cannot redefine the Codex version format or be compared across namespaces.', E'27f8244a9261b82be23801100df5a4bd1b5c8d22e404034bf60041498a12530e', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D84', E'CODEX_MODULE_FOUNDATION', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'canonical-timestamp-envelope-successor', E'canonical-timestamp-envelope-successor\nSUCCESSOR:D79 is superseded. TIMESTAMP-ONLY:this article governs timestamp fields,clock evidence,normalization and correction and never defines or evolves a version number. PROFILE:each immutable event,evidence,audit or revision record applies the registered timestamp profile for that record type. The minimum canonical envelope contains recorded_at_utc,source_clock_id,precision,timestamp_status and timestamp_hash;occurred_at_utc,observed_at_utc,effective_at_utc,expires_at_utc,time_zone,utc_offset,monotonic_sequence and clock_skew_ms are required when their declared semantics apply. FORMAT:canonical UTC values use YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss.ffffffZ,Gregorian calendar,24-hour UTC,six fractional digits and uppercase Z. STATUS:verified|estimated|corrected|invalid. SEPARATION:timestamp values are immutable evidence values allowed by D82;field/schema/status definitions are canonical declarations,not consumer hardcoding. A timestamp cannot act as a version,release identity,generation or ordering authority except that monotonic_sequence resolves equal/regressed wall-clock observations. LEGACY-MIGRATION:legacy timestamp rows retain the original value and append canonical_recorded_at_utc,timestamp_status and immutable migration evidence;date-only revision history is estimated at the declared UTC boundary and cannot claim occurrence precision. CORRECTION:never overwrite source evidence;append or store a paired canonical successor with reason,authority and correlation. VALIDATION:permission-sovereign validates timestamp evidence admissibility while 星澄 independently inspects Codex/implementation agreement.\nFORBID:version rule inside timestamp article+timestamp as version+version as timestamp+naive canonical time+omitted six-digit fraction+numeric-offset canonical storage+invented occurrence precision+overwriting legacy source value+unregistered clock+hidden clock regression+invalid timestamp blocking unrelated scope.\nA source that cannot prove occurrence time records estimated status and uncertainty. A non-expiring record may omit expires_at_utc only when its registered timestamp profile declares non-expiry.', E'6b9d9eb0fbd67ca64432df73f3498a2f61e1946ec96a5d98966fc719713aba6c', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D85', E'CODEX_MODULE_FOUNDATION', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'timestamp-version-cross-codex-separation-interpretation', E'timestamp-version-cross-codex-separation-interpretation\nINTERPRETATION:D84 is the sole current timestamp representation rule and D83 is the sole current version-number rule. Earlier provisions including D30,C57 and C67 remain effective only for their domain duties;their words time,timestamp,expiry,version,generation or release reference the applicable typed authority and do not establish another format. D82 governs only value-reference placement. PRECEDENCE:on representation conflict D84 controls timestamps and D83 controls versions;neither controls the other\'s namespace. REFERENCES:new provisions,registries,commands and contracts cite the applicable article instead of restating formats. CHECKERS:emit separate findings for timestamp violation and version violation even when one record contains both.\nFORBID:implicit mixed timestamp-version type+restated competing format+one finding concealing two violations+legacy wording overriding D84/D83+timestamp correction changing version+version evolution rewriting timestamp evidence.\nA historical provision remains immutable evidence;this interpretation narrows only its current application and does not rewrite historical text.', E'd1f3bc46e196ab8e6bbf71dff569098982119be3dd50918d728f6694ef4c0dc3', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D86', E'CODEX_MODULE_FOUNDATION', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'timestamp-derived-version-identity-successor', E'timestamp-derived-version-identity-successor\nSUCCESSOR:D83 is superseded. VERSION-IDENTITY:every new Codex,application,tool,release,contract,schema,ABI,governance-schema and runtime-generation version is a UTC timestamp identity formatted YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ssZ. The registered issuing authority assigns it once at seal or activation;the value is immutable,unique within its namespace and ordered as UTC time. This replaces creation of new decimal or semantic numeric versions. SEPARATION:this article governs version identity only;D90 governs event/evidence timestamps. A version timestamp is not occurred_at_utc,recorded_at_utc or file modification time even when values coincide. COLLISION:multiple releases in one second append the registered monotonic sequence as a separate identity component;they do not fabricate time. LEGACY:1.00000 and earlier numeric values remain read-only aliases and lineage evidence only;they cannot select,order or activate current state. EXTERNAL:upstream dependency versions remain descriptive evidence and bind to a local timestamp version identity. AUTOMATION:no repair,update,model or checker may infer or rewrite a version from mtime,Git,build,filename or cache.\n\nPACKAGE-AUTO-DEFER:每24小時偵測一次。未具明確新增套件許可者自動標記DEFERRED_AWAITING_PERMISSION；一般新版發布未滿14日者自動標記DEFERRED_OBSERVATION_WINDOW。遞延不等於拒絕、通過或已安裝，遞延期間禁止下載、安裝、鎖定或執行；條件成熟後於下一次週期自動重新評估。重大安全或相容性事件得立即加跑受管檢查。\nFORBID:new numeric version authority+semantic-version increment for GPTBridge identity+mtime/Git/build/cache-derived version+event timestamp silently reused as version+cross-namespace comparison+timestamp-version overwrite+legacy numeric alias selecting current state+fabricated collision time.\nLegacy consumers may read preserved numeric aliases during migration but every newly issued identity and activation record uses the timestamp version.', E'2b3ef180c96c385b0146f9380424622fa1cd1bf4a242223ed58e1ea70bf947b6', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D87', E'CODEX_MODULE_FOUNDATION', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'timestamp-version-separation-interpretation-successor', E'timestamp-version-separation-interpretation-successor\nSUCCESSOR:D85 is superseded. INTERPRETATION:D86 exclusively defines timestamp-derived version identities;D90 exclusively defines event,evidence,audit and revision timestamp envelopes;D89 exclusively defines code and environment reference placement. Earlier provisions retain domain duties but establish no competing version or timestamp format. The word version in a current operational rule resolves to a typed D86 timestamp version unless explicitly marked legacy_version_alias. The word timestamp resolves to an D90 evidence field unless explicitly marked version_identity. CHECKERS:version identity misuse and evidence timestamp misuse are separate findings with exact table,field,file and expected authority.\nFORBID:one untyped timestamp field serving both version and evidence+legacy text overriding current successor+mixed finding hiding two violations+event-time correction changing version identity+version activation rewriting event evidence.\nHistorical provisions and values remain immutable evidence;this successor changes only current interpretation.', E'43bd592505716034250a043dccd5c7cdf9046b6473f6fff91fdcf667f0df34f1', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D88', E'CODEX_MODULE_MAINTENANCE', E'CODEX_AUTOMATIC_REPAIR_SPECIAL_LAW', E'automatic-command-contract-timestamp-version-successor', E'automatic-command-contract-timestamp-version-successor\nSUCCESSOR:C70 is superseded. COMMAND-SET:the registered repair/update switch,confirmation,revocation and approved-execution commands remain exhaustive. DOMAIN-SCOPE:for faults of the C105 internal domain no user-facing pending confirmation is produced, so the repair-side switch/confirmation/execution commands are inert for that domain; they remain registered and effective for the user-facing domain. CONTRACT-VERSION:each request and response contract has a canonical contract_version_identity issued under D86. Existing identifiers ending -v1 are legacy aliases only and resolve through command_contract_revision_registry;no new -v2 or numeric contract suffix is created. CONTRACT-RECORD:contract_id,legacy_alias,version_identity,request_schema,response_schema,owner,content_hash,status and predecessor_contract_id are mandatory. ROLE-SEPARATION:user decides switch/confirmation/revocation;星澄 presents and records;permission-sovereign validates permission and evidence;automation-sovereign decides synchronized dispatch;module execution alone mutates. GATE:enabled matching switch,current unrevoked single-use confirmation,permission proof,synchronization decision,before hash and generation are all required. Action/evidence timestamps use D90 fields separately from contract_version_identity.\nFORBID:new numeric contract version+unregistered alias+implicit consent+confirmation reuse+missing revocation+permission execution+synchronization module work+executor scope expansion+contract version confused with action time.\nLegacy -v1 aliases remain readable during bounded migration but cannot identify a newly issued contract.', E'0e7e17175bd5576fc9c2213a4bb1ccc72f56d04420cb4a2c35e44fdbbb06ef48', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D89', E'CODEX_MODULE_FOUNDATION', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'dynamic-reference-policy-timestamp-version-successor', E'dynamic-reference-policy-timestamp-version-successor\nSUCCESSOR:D82 is superseded. GENERAL:operational values are consumed through typed canonical codes or governed environment bindings. Canonical registry declarations,legal schema definitions,code identities,immutable D90 evidence timestamps and sealed D86 version identities are authoritative definitions rather than duplicated consumer hardcoding. SEPARATION:D86 defines version identity,D90 defines evidence timestamp,D89 defines only reference placement. Consumers never restate paths,endpoints,models,limits,states,contracts or identities. CHECKING:each finding names the literal,semantic class,expected authority and exact file or Codex field. Historical literals remain evidence and are not copied forward.\nFORBID:duplicated operational literal+canonical definition treated as consumer hardcoding+invented whitelist+timestamp format restated outside D90+version semantics restated outside D86+legacy number used as current identity.\nRegistered fixtures and third-party/generated evidence remain bounded and non-authoritative.', E'064c8803fa289c4027007659f7489f8d52c304d1da28acbf53f1b3e1061dc337', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D9', E'CODEX_MODULE_FOUNDATION', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'absolute-codex-immutability', E'absolute-codex-immutability\nSEALED-VERSION:read-only+content-addressed+permanently-preserved; ACTOR-WITH-MUTATION-POWER:none; REVISION:create-new-complete-version+new-digest+new-seal-only; PRIOR-VERSION:unchanged\nFORBID:any-update/delete/patch/append/rewrite/schema-mutation/in-place-migration/restore-overwrite/hot-update/repair/database-write/trigger/procedure/tool-write/runtime-write/human-direct-edit-to-sealed-codex\nCreating and sealing a distinct complete successor version is not modification of an existing sealed version.', E'8d924181d0c6846db1e95510b6fbf5cda3f87557260d5551f6d4413dc1680ae6', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D90', E'CODEX_MODULE_FOUNDATION', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'canonical-evidence-timestamp-envelope-successor', E'canonical-evidence-timestamp-envelope-successor\nSUCCESSOR:D84 is superseded. EVIDENCE-TIMESTAMP:this article governs event,evidence,audit and revision times,not version identity. Canonical UTC fields use YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss.ffffffZ with six fractional digits and uppercase Z. Applicable profiles use occurred_at_utc,recorded_at_utc,observed_at_utc,effective_at_utc,expires_at_utc,source_clock_id,precision,timestamp_status,timestamp_hash,monotonic_sequence,clock_skew_ms,time_zone and utc_offset. STATUS:verified|estimated|corrected|invalid. VERSION-SEPARATION:version_identity is governed by D86 and stored in a different typed field;an evidence timestamp cannot activate or order versions. LEGACY:original values remain and canonical companions plus migration evidence are appended;estimated values never claim original precision. VALIDATION:permission-sovereign validates admissibility while 星澄 independently inspects compliance.\nFORBID:evidence timestamp used as version+version identity used as occurrence time+missing fractional precision+naive canonical time+overwrite+fabricated precision+unregistered clock+hidden regression+invalid time blocking unrelated scope.\nA record lacking provable occurrence time uses estimated status;non-expiry is allowed only through its registered profile.', E'eb7e1c0a02fd264842e955938a5e6fec68537ff6da3ffb2ce5a342335ac0754d', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D91', E'CODEX_MODULE_FOUNDATION', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'timestamp-version-issuance-and-collision-successor', E'timestamp-version-issuance-and-collision-successor\nIDENTITY:formal contract,schema,rule,release and runtime names contain no version number;GENERATION:the authority records an internal UTC timestamp for ordering,lineage,collision prevention and rollback,without exposing it in the formal identity or normative prose;ISSUE:each namespace has one strictly later current generation;COLLISION:wait for a later internal timestamp;PROHIBITION:no decimal,semantic,ordinal or visible timestamp suffix in identity names.\nFORBID:more than one version per namespace per second+composite version unsupported by parser+monotonic sequence embedded in version+new numeric increment+severity encoded in timestamp+fabricated future second+mtime/Git/build/cache-derived version+legacy alias selecting active state.\n', E'39aaa91f3fd2eadf28cc4d5359361f9df9d2ec82aae325847837389b61cc8fbd', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D92', E'CODEX_MODULE_FOUNDATION', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'timestamp-version-change-classification-successor', E'timestamp-version-change-classification-successor\nCLASSIFICATION:change classes express impact and required review only;GENERATION:successor ordering and lineage use the internal authority timestamp and never alter the stable formal identity;COMPATIBILITY:owner-local contracts declare compatibility and migration outside normative prose;PROHIBITION:no version increment arithmetic or visible version token.\nFORBID:version addition+decimal increment+floating-point comparison+change severity inferred from timestamp distance+timestamp fabricated to encode class+legacy increment table used for current issuance+automatic classification changing law.\n', E'c45923c7f7e1bb292c3729f82f769a32025e43ac8ebf4c6d420bc6e4c15cc2fe', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D93', E'CODEX_MODULE_FOUNDATION', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'timestamp-version-ledger-and-recovery-integrity', E'timestamp-version-ledger-and-recovery-integrity\nLEDGER:revision_history remains append-only across a version-format migration and cannot be cleared,restarted or replaced. A recovered row is marked corrected or estimated,identifies its source evidence and never claims verified status unless its original signed record is proven. VERSION-MIGRATION:each transition record preserves legacy version,canonical timestamp version,recorded evidence time,previous hash,entry hash and recovery evidence. SEAL:the current seal history_head must equal the latest revision and its timestamp version must equal metadata codex_version and the Chinese artifact codex_version. REGISTRIES:version_evolution_rules is legacy-retired;timestamp_version_evolution_rules is current. FAILURE:missing history,head mismatch,unproven verified recovery,non-increasing timestamp version or active numeric increment is a Codex issue and blocks a new seal without stopping unrelated runtime review.\nFORBID:revision-history deletion+sequence restart+recovered evidence marked verified without proof+seal/head/version mismatch+active numeric increment+silent version migration+rewriting original legacy row.\nA missing historical record may be represented by an explicit gap finding until evidence supports correction;inventing its content is forbidden.', E'50b4fdde1f16dec43faccc521c7fe242360fe2d3681abdbaddd426b934ffc4ee', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D94', E'CODEX_MODULE_FOUNDATION', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'active-successor-reference-and-legacy-binding-closure', E'active-successor-reference-and-legacy-binding-closure\nREFERENCE-RESOLUTION:every current reference to a superseded provision resolves through provision_reference_resolution to exactly one active successor before interpretation;the predecessor remains historical identity only. A reference inside a SUCCESSOR declaration is historical evidence and is not an active dependency. CURRENT-MAP:D86 resolves to D91 for timestamp version identity;D83 resolves through D86 to D91;D84 resolves to D90 for evidence timestamps;D82 resolves to D89 for dynamic references;C70 resolves to D88 for automatic command contracts;D85 resolves to D87 for cross-Codex interpretation;D15 and D19 resolve to D92 for change classification. BINDING:legacy numeric effective_version values are preserved in legacy_effective_version while current_binding_version points to the current timestamp version;this binds existing active provisions without fabricating their original effective time. STATUS:timestamp_status uses only verified,estimated,corrected or invalid. HISTORY:revision_history remains empty under C72 and this amendment is represented by provision lineage,current seal and canonical timestamp only.\n\nPACKAGE-AUTO-DEFER:每24小時偵測一次。未具明確新增套件許可者自動標記DEFERRED_AWAITING_PERMISSION；一般新版發布未滿14日者自動標記DEFERRED_OBSERVATION_WINDOW。遞延不等於拒絕、通過或已安裝，遞延期間禁止下載、安裝、鎖定或執行；條件成熟後於下一次週期自動重新評估。重大安全或相容性事件得立即加跑受管檢查。\nFORBID:interpreting superseded text without successor resolution+multiple active successors+rewriting historical effective version+numeric legacy field selecting current law+timestamp status outside canonical vocabulary+repopulating user-deleted revision history.\nA deliberately historical citation may address the predecessor when explicitly marked historical and cannot control current operation.', E'af73880dbecd69187bc86d4e0cfa026d8ad8d0d54e7d03a94276ff6f09888b07', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D95', E'CODEX_MODULE_FOUNDATION', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'codex-search-index-freshness-and-query-plan-gate', E'codex-search-index-freshness-and-query-plan-gate\nSEARCH-MANIFEST:every search generation records search_schema_id,Codex version identity,authoritative content root,source_count,indexed_count,FTS tokenizer,module-manifest root,index-content hash,built_at_utc and status. FRESHNESS:a search result is usable only when manifest version and content root equal the current seal,source_count equals provision identities,indexed_count equals search documents and the source row content hash matches authoritative content. QUERY-PLAN:exact identity uses a unique index;module/law/lifecycle filters use composite indexes;short registered Chinese aliases use codex_search_alias;free text of supported length uses local FTS. The planner never converts a failed exact lookup into an unbounded scan. REBUILD:Codex amendment rebuilds changed documents and FTS atomically before sealing;corrupt or stale derived indexes are discarded and rebuilt without modifying authority. BENCHMARK:record cold/warm duration,result count,query class,plan identity and version for bounded diagnostics;performance numbers are monitoring evidence only. CONFIDENTIALITY:no Chinese mirror content,RAG,Rust-Vector-Engine,network or external process enters the search index.\nFORBID:search without fresh manifest+source/index count drift+content-root mismatch+unindexed interactive scan+FTS as authority+stale result after amendment+external or RAG indexing+Chinese mirror ingestion+benchmark changing governance outcome.\nA maintenance integrity scan may bypass search indexes to verify or rebuild them,while clearly marked non-interactive and non-authoritative.', E'91413aecf3566540518aa4ca0d29cbc95fb08327f45c4c2ce2c1720218379531', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D96', E'CODEX_MODULE_LANGUAGE', E'CODEX_LANGUAGE_SOURCE_NATIVE_SPECIAL_LAW', E'module-self-decomposition-command-state-and-exception-closure', E'module-self-decomposition-command-state-and-exception-closure\nSCOPE:all B95 decomposition work; COMMAND:MODULE_SELF_DECOMPOSE with canonical id module-self-decompose is the sole mutation entry and is dispatched by 星澄 auxiliary automation coordinator through the information layer after permission scope validation; STATE-MACHINE:DETECTED>PLANNED>AUTHORIZED>STAGING>VERIFYING>PROMOTED,with BLOCKED|FAILED>ROLLED_BACK and exact transition evidence;no state may be inferred from elapsed time,file presence or process exit alone; IDENTITY:each job binds decomposition_id+module_code+owner+task_id+source_revision+base_content_root+target_paths+contract_hash+dependency_graph_hash+generation+correlation_id+requested_at_utc+authorization proof;queue entry is immutable and execution targets the bound revision,never a moving branch; AUTHORIZATION:an explicit current user one-time command is legal authorization for its exact scope;automatic recurring execution requires a separate registered user-controlled switch and cannot be inferred from this one-time request; EXCEPTION-CLOSURE:source_exceptions grants no line-limit waiver after B93;all authored registry,policy,governance,test,migration,launcher and generator sources obey the same limits;legacy exception rows are retired from effective authority; VERIFICATION:result binds child module identities+before/after hashes+line-count evidence+API/ABI/contract parity+dependency acyclicity+tests+resource budget+old-root removal+audit validation;only complete evidence permits PROMOTED; REPORT:each failure names exact file+symbol+rule+fault code+state+expected+observed+owner+next action and never reports a generic decomposition failure; CODEX-DERIVED-EVIDENCE:every amendment refreshes manifests+FTS+benchmarks+search seal atomically; HISTORY:revision_history remains user-deleted.\n\nPACKAGE-AUTO-DEFER:每24小時偵測一次。未具明確新增套件許可者自動標記DEFERRED_AWAITING_PERMISSION；一般新版發布未滿14日者自動標記DEFERRED_OBSERVATION_WINDOW。遞延不等於拒絕、通過或已安裝，遞延期間禁止下載、安裝、鎖定或執行；條件成熟後於下一次週期自動重新評估。重大安全或相容性事件得立即加跑受管檢查。\nFORBID:alternate decomposition command+direct subprocess/editor mutation+moving branch target+implicit or expired authorization+recurring automation from one-time command+line-limit exception registry+generic failure+state skipping+promotion with stale/missing evidence+old-root retention+checker repair+permission-sovereign execution+星澄 direct source execution+history reconstruction.\nNo authored-source exception exists. An immutable third-party or generated artifact classification does not exempt its GPTBridge-authored generator, wrapper or adapter.', E'dfb68dec686c02a226dfc23474005023c77523f5ffbc6c037fd1ac1fdf46b615', E'superseded', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D97', E'CODEX_MODULE_DIRECTORY', E'CODEX_DIRECTORY_SPECIAL_LAW', E'source-line-evidence-and-self-decomposition-directory-special-law', E'source-line-evidence-and-self-decomposition-directory-special-law\nDIRECTORIES:DIR_SOURCE_LINE_LIMIT_EVIDENCE and DIR_MODULE_SELF_DECOMPOSITION are the sole normalized directories for B93-D96 measurements and jobs; OWNER:permission-sovereign owns identity,format,registration,lifecycle and validation only; PRODUCERS:read-only language checkers submit measured evidence and 星澄 submits classification+plan+dispatch evidence through the information layer;module executors submit execution results;none may register,validate or rewrite its own record; LINE-EVIDENCE:one record binds evidence_id+module_code+canonical source code/path reference+language+source_class+symbol_kind+symbol_identity+effective_lines+limit+content_hash+source_revision+parser/checker/policy versions+result+timestamp+lineage; DECOMPOSITION-JOB:one record binds decomposition_id+module_code+violation evidence ids+state+owner+task+source revision+candidate revision+target codes+locked paths/contracts/state owners/artifacts+authorization+resource budget+attempt+fault codes+verification hashes+audit+timestamps+lineage; CARDINALITY:each active over-limit evidence belongs to exactly one current module and zero-or-one open decomposition job;one job may resolve many violations in that same module;cross-module work uses separately linked jobs; LIFECYCLE:evidence is append-only and becomes resolved|superseded|stale without overwrite;job transitions follow D96 and every transition is a new event;PROMOTED requires all bound violations resolved by current after-evidence; FRESHNESS:source,parser,checker,policy,contract,dependency graph or module generation hash change marks affected evidence stale and blocks reuse;unknown or missing registry state is INCOMPLETE_EVIDENCE; SEARCH:exact evidence/job/module/state/fault/revision lookup uses indexed coded fields;free text is never identity; RETENTION:records remain through release and audit retention then archive with hash-chain continuity; HISTORY:revision_history remains user-deleted.\n\nPACKAGE-AUTO-DEFER:每24小時偵測一次。未具明確新增套件許可者自動標記DEFERRED_AWAITING_PERMISSION；一般新版發布未滿14日者自動標記DEFERRED_OBSERVATION_WINDOW。遞延不等於拒絕、通過或已安裝，遞延期間禁止下載、安裝、鎖定或執行；條件成熟後於下一次週期自動重新評估。重大安全或相容性事件得立即加跑受管檢查。\nFORBID:local/private exception list+free-text-only identity+path literal as authority+self-registration+self-validation+mutable evidence overwrite+one job silently spanning unrelated modules+multiple open jobs for same module generation+stale evidence reuse+state inferred from process/file presence+PROMOTED with unresolved violation+deleting failure evidence+directory content creating or relaxing Codex law.\nRead-only historical records may be archived after governed retention; archival never native-javascript-esmivates evidence, authorizes execution or removes the current compliance requirement.', E'e90eda5bf0a705e62882932cec13c316d4c7098a98d9f00f82578e42466853b7', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D98', E'CODEX_MODULE_FOUNDATION', E'CODEX_MAIN', E'formal-rule-contract-and-precedence-convergence', E'formal-rule-contract-and-precedence-convergence\nFORMALIZATION:natural-language provisions state intent but each machine-enforced invariant must bind one formal_rule_code with typed inputs,predicate,decision,severity,evidence schema,applicability,low-cost path and controlling provision. PRECEDENCE:exact special-law scope>later explicit successor>subordinate ordinance>general article;provision_reference_resolution_v2 records successor/clarification and special_law_conflict_matrix records scoped overrides;an unresolved apparent conflict is INCOMPLETE_EVIDENCE,never left to checker interpretation. DEDUPLICATION:one formal rule owns each repeated boundary;other provisions reference its code and add only scoped fields. CHANGE:predicate or decision semantic change requires successor/version;checker code cannot invent policy. PROOF:formal evaluation records rule_code,input hashes,result,evidence ids,policy version and timestamp.\nFORBID:natural-language substring as executable policy+same invariant implemented by multiple divergent checkers+precedence guessed from article number+later text silently overriding special law+unresolved conflict accepted+missing formal rule treated PASS.\nPure explanatory or historical text need not become executable,provided it cannot change a gate,permission,state or release decision.', E'9cb54b6afad07e485b65ca4abc7894c4e6adef3fe5d37d611c5c62a696e6bf92', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
INSERT INTO "codex_search_document" ("provision_type", "provision_id", "module_code", "law_code", "subject", "content", "content_hash", "lifecycle_state", "version_identity") VALUES (E'article', E'D99', E'CODEX_MODULE_AUDIT', E'CODEX_AUDIT_EVIDENCE_TIME_SPECIAL_LAW', E'receipt-token-and-audit-event-machine-schemas', E'receipt-token-and-audit-event-machine-schemas\nCANONICAL-CONTRACTS:receipt contract+token contract+audit-event contract+gate-evidence contract;AUDIT_EVENT:event_id+sequence+previous_event_hash+event_type+actor+role+operation+target+scope+result+technical_status+certification_status+finding_code+severity+failure_classification+fault_codes+evidence_refs+revision_before/after+generation+occurred/recorded+correlation/causation+redaction_class+event_hash;AUTOMATION:C++23 Audit Engine and registered native check providers emit schema-valid events;unsupported checks produce BLOCKED and deny release;VALIDATION:schema+version+type+requiredness+chain+scope+generation+evidence freshness before gate use;PYTHON:none\nFORBID:Python-audit-event-producer+Python-delegated-check+free-form-audit-payload+missing-status/finding/severity/failure-classification+silent-unsupported-check+broken-chain+generic-success\nA no-op pure internal call needs no execution receipt;optional trace events remain non-authoritative and content-redacted.', E'9b9b4c9776a6e9a9c25a7d298cb0724b4d1d27dbe2c0754a0335332685d41df9', E'active', E'2026-10-01T16:43:07Z');
